WEBVTT

00:01.346 --> 00:04.831
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:04.866 --> 00:08.165
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:08.201 --> 00:11.915
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:11.951 --> 00:14.919
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:14.954 --> 00:18.323
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:18.357 --> 00:21.691
<i>Lucky there's a man who
positively can do</i>

00:21.727 --> 00:23.318
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:23.362 --> 00:24.962
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:24.998 --> 00:30.335
<i>He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy!</i>

00:40.199 --> 00:42.200
Whoa, whoa, easy, boy, easy.

00:42.234 --> 00:44.702
I-It's just Stewie in a kitty costume.

00:44.737 --> 00:47.171
I'm a calico, and my name is Humphrey.

00:47.206 --> 00:49.307
He got his face painted
at a birthday party.

00:49.341 --> 00:51.542
It was the only thing
this little guy could do.

00:51.577 --> 00:53.344
He was too light
for the caterpillar slide,

00:53.378 --> 00:55.012
<i>too short for the piГ±ata,</i>

00:55.047 --> 00:57.348
and too scared to touch
the animals in the petting zoo.

00:57.382 --> 00:59.584
- Half of them had erections.
- Half of them had erections.

00:59.618 --> 01:00.952
The pony was magnificent.

01:00.986 --> 01:04.188
The pony was magnificent.

01:04.223 --> 01:06.257
- Oh, what do we have here?
- Hey, back off!

01:06.291 --> 01:07.458
That's my goodie bag.

01:08.460 --> 01:10.261
Ugh. An eraser.

01:10.295 --> 01:12.997
Raisins in an unsealed sandwich bag.

01:13.031 --> 01:14.699
Oh, a parachute guy.

01:14.733 --> 01:17.268
Uhp, he's already tangled.

01:17.302 --> 01:19.036
This day started off so great.

01:19.071 --> 01:21.339
It was awash in cake and pony boners.

01:21.373 --> 01:23.574
Now all I have is this dumb whistle.

01:23.609 --> 01:24.675
Doesn't even work.

01:26.845 --> 01:28.246
Ow! What the hell?!

01:28.280 --> 01:30.081
Oh, it's a dog whistle.

01:32.084 --> 01:34.252
I've always wondered
what that sounds like to you.

01:36.021 --> 01:38.556
<i>Dog whistle! Dog whistle!</i>

01:38.590 --> 01:40.992
<i>Where are you, dog?!</i>

01:41.026 --> 01:42.226
- Give me that!
- Hey.

01:42.261 --> 01:43.594
Oh, what, you want it? Here, take it.

01:43.629 --> 01:45.029
Give it back.

01:45.063 --> 01:47.331
- Give me it.
- No. It's mine now.

01:47.366 --> 01:50.101
In fact, I'm gonna put it
where you can never reach it.

01:50.135 --> 01:51.269
No!

01:51.303 --> 01:53.704
Good luck, shrimp.

01:55.407 --> 01:57.809
I can't believe the nerve of that dog.

01:57.843 --> 01:59.811
Teaching me a lesson about size?

01:59.845 --> 02:02.246
I'm not even that small.

02:02.281 --> 02:03.981
Tiny Tom Cruise?

02:04.016 --> 02:06.250
Oh, hey, little guy.
Forgot my sunglasses.

02:06.285 --> 02:08.753
Hey, what's with
your gay character names lately?

02:08.787 --> 02:10.655
Stacee Jaxx? Jack Reacher?

02:10.689 --> 02:12.223
I mean, who are you playing next?

02:12.257 --> 02:14.692
All right, try to make this sound gay:

02:14.726 --> 02:17.261
next up, I play Headmaster Bates Mann.

02:17.296 --> 02:18.896
- Anything else?
- Actually, yes.

02:18.931 --> 02:22.033
After that, I'll be taking
the role of Major Dixon Butts,

02:22.067 --> 02:24.235
then Senator Rod Clutcher.

02:33.579 --> 02:35.947
I'm too small, am I, Brian?

02:35.981 --> 02:38.482
Well, we'll just see
who's the bigger man.

02:38.517 --> 02:42.486
"Brian, sorry I got testy.
Let's bury the hatchet.

02:42.521 --> 02:44.779
"If you're free, I'd love to hear about

02:44.815 --> 02:46.178
any new writing projects
you're working..."

02:46.179 --> 02:48.826
Oh, at least wait for me to send it.

02:50.295 --> 02:52.897
Hey, Stewie, I got your text.
What am I working on?

02:52.931 --> 02:54.932
<i>What am I not working on?</i>

02:54.967 --> 02:57.301
Well, first off, I got this
screenplay for Tom Cruise,

02:57.336 --> 03:00.371
about the queen's private
secretary, Sir Gaylord Hummer.

03:00.405 --> 03:02.006
Well, actually, he might do that.

03:02.040 --> 03:06.410
<i>But, Brian, I'm more interested
in short stories.</i>

03:26.298 --> 03:28.900
Well, hello there, little guy.

03:28.934 --> 03:30.468
What the hell did you do to me, Stewie?

03:30.502 --> 03:32.737
Well, Brian, you seemed
to enjoy belittling me,

03:32.771 --> 03:34.572
so I decided to belittle you.

03:34.606 --> 03:36.674
I've simply shrunken down
your molecular structure.

03:36.708 --> 03:38.376
It was easy, really.

03:38.410 --> 03:41.946
Like taking candy,
or a whistle, from a baby.

03:41.980 --> 03:43.714
You dick. Undo this.

03:43.749 --> 03:45.349
This is perfect.

03:45.384 --> 03:47.118
I think my excitement is best expressed

03:47.152 --> 03:49.820
by Jean-Claude Van Damme in this scene.

04:01.934 --> 04:04.135
All right, you've made
your point. I'm sorry.

04:04.169 --> 04:06.103
I'm sorry I couldn't hear that,
it's too high-pitched.

04:06.138 --> 04:07.505
- You're what?
- I'm sorry.

04:07.539 --> 04:09.340
- For what?
- For calling you a shrimp.

04:09.374 --> 04:11.142
- And?
- What do you mean "and"?

04:11.176 --> 04:13.177
Come on, you know what I want.

04:13.211 --> 04:15.346
And... all four chairs

04:15.380 --> 04:17.982
<i>would totally turn for you on The Voice.</i>

04:18.016 --> 04:19.984
Anything else?

04:20.018 --> 04:22.386
And the way you salute
and point is very casual

04:22.421 --> 04:24.522
and free of affectation.

04:24.556 --> 04:27.024
Hey, thanks, Bri.
I'll go switch you back.

04:36.535 --> 04:38.336
Stewie!

04:38.370 --> 04:39.704
You know, I'm really flattered you think

04:39.738 --> 04:41.973
<i>all four Voice chairs would turn around.</i>

04:42.007 --> 04:44.408
My dream order would be Adam, Blake,

04:44.443 --> 04:46.444
Alicia Keys, and then Kelly Clarkson,

04:46.478 --> 04:48.746
whose chair I imagine would turn last,

04:48.780 --> 04:52.416
'cause she's, uh... she's a bigger gal.

04:52.451 --> 04:54.118
Help!

04:55.220 --> 04:57.054
Oh, crap.

04:57.089 --> 04:59.090
Don't worry, Brian, I'll save you!

04:59.124 --> 05:01.392
But I'm a millennial,
so first I have to watch

05:01.426 --> 05:03.961
a YouTube instructional video
on how to do it.

05:03.996 --> 05:05.396
<i>What's going on, guys?</i>

05:05.430 --> 05:07.164
<i>I'm Corey, and today I'm gonna teach you</i>

05:07.199 --> 05:09.166
<i>how to get your friend
out of a rat hole.</i>

05:09.201 --> 05:11.235
<i>Now, before we get started,
don't forget to subscribe</i>

05:11.269 --> 05:12.903
<i>to my channel, Corey's World.</i>

05:12.938 --> 05:15.573
<i>And, guys, I'll get to
as many comments as I can,</i>

05:15.607 --> 05:17.241
but I can't get to all of them.

05:17.275 --> 05:19.076
<i>And don't forget to check out
my other videos,</i>

05:19.111 --> 05:20.578
<i>like "How to Play Guitar."</i>

05:20.612 --> 05:22.613
Uh, Brian, this might be a while.

05:22.647 --> 05:24.815
<i>What's going on, guys? I'm Corey.</i>

05:30.409 --> 05:32.965
Brian! Hang in there, buddy.

05:32.999 --> 05:35.467
Hurry up! Get this rat away from me!

05:35.502 --> 05:37.503
I'll shrink myself down
and come get you.

05:37.537 --> 05:39.305
But in the meantime, they say

05:39.339 --> 05:41.907
if you put your finger in
a rat's butt, that disables it.

05:43.610 --> 05:45.578
It didn't work. Now he's just angry.

05:45.612 --> 05:47.513
Try wetting your finger first.

05:47.547 --> 05:50.683
Just get in here!

06:01.494 --> 06:04.196
Hey, come on, guy.
Hey, you don't want to do this.

06:12.606 --> 06:14.974
I'll have what she's having.

06:18.378 --> 06:19.678
Please tell me that's not the finger

06:19.713 --> 06:21.313
you stuck in a rat's butt.

06:21.348 --> 06:24.016
No. It... I don't-I don't
remember which one it was.

06:24.050 --> 06:25.818
Yeah, that was the finger.

06:25.852 --> 06:28.988
All right, let's get back
to the machine.

06:29.022 --> 06:30.990
Look at all this shag carpet.

06:31.024 --> 06:32.992
This is like our Vietnam movie.

06:33.026 --> 06:35.127
I miss Jenny.

06:35.161 --> 06:38.230
- What is that?
- That's Forrest. Forrest Gump.

06:38.265 --> 06:40.399
- Yeah, I-I don't think so.
- Shh.

06:40.433 --> 06:43.002
What is that?

06:43.036 --> 06:45.838
It ain't a box of chocolates.

06:47.440 --> 06:49.441
Vacuum cleaner!

06:55.315 --> 07:00.052
I hate my life and nobody
can hear me say it right now!

07:15.835 --> 07:18.470
Oh, my God, this is disgusting!

07:18.505 --> 07:20.172
I just hope she's done vacuuming.

07:20.206 --> 07:21.740
Okay, everyone,

07:21.775 --> 07:24.376
dump your toenails in the hall,
I'm vacuuming.

07:24.411 --> 07:26.512
Oh, God.

07:33.086 --> 07:35.087
That was close.

07:48.935 --> 07:51.303
Oh, my God, we're in the trash outside!

07:51.338 --> 07:54.573
We've got to get down from here.
Quick, pass me that baggie.

08:00.080 --> 08:02.448
How am I supposed to get down?
That was the only baggie.

08:02.482 --> 08:03.882
Use either the tampon strings

08:03.917 --> 08:06.719
or the discarded dental floss
and rappel down.

08:09.055 --> 08:10.856
Which one did you go with?

08:10.890 --> 08:13.625
Neither. I was hoping to kill myself.

08:16.296 --> 08:19.198
Two days of mail at once, nobody knows.

08:19.232 --> 08:22.057
Don't go over two. Don't get greedy.

08:22.902 --> 08:25.104
Uhp, got a bat in the cave.

08:25.138 --> 08:27.106
All right, I figure if we can just...

08:27.140 --> 08:28.907
What's going on? An eclipse?

08:28.942 --> 08:31.543
- Ah! Oh, my God! Oh, my God!
- Holy crap! What is that?!

08:31.578 --> 08:33.479
- Gross! Oh!
- What is on us? Oh!

08:35.682 --> 08:37.683
Ah! Snot rocket!

08:37.717 --> 08:39.752
Oh, my God, it's so disgusting!

08:39.786 --> 08:41.754
Get it off! Get it off!

08:41.788 --> 08:44.590
- Are you guys eating that?
- Uh, what?

08:44.624 --> 08:47.593
Are you eating this pile of boogers?

08:47.627 --> 08:50.529
- Uh, no.
- Can I eat it?

08:50.563 --> 08:52.965
Yeah, please. We're stuck.

08:52.999 --> 08:56.368
Dude, dude, you got to get down
here, by the big trash can.

08:56.403 --> 08:58.370
Dude, dude, dude, just get here.

09:01.508 --> 09:04.543
- Brian, we've got to get up to my room.
- Yeah, but how?

09:04.577 --> 09:06.912
We'll just climb the lattice
on the front of the house.

09:08.681 --> 09:11.316
- When did we get that?
- Well, every '80s movie had one,

09:11.351 --> 09:13.752
so the fat man thought
we should have one, too.

09:13.787 --> 09:17.256
Wow. Okay, great.

09:17.290 --> 09:19.158
You know, it's funny,
you said "every '80s movie,"

09:19.192 --> 09:20.959
but I can't think of a single one.

09:20.994 --> 09:23.128
<i>- Ferris Bueller's Day Off?
- I don't think so.</i>

09:23.163 --> 09:25.597
But the lattice thing
sounded right when you said it.

09:25.632 --> 09:28.100
I-I feel like '80s movies
were wall-to-wall lattices.

09:28.134 --> 09:30.969
<i>- Sixteen Candles?
- Hmm... no, no.</i>

09:31.004 --> 09:33.105
I mean, she was being ignored
most of the movie.

09:33.139 --> 09:34.673
Who'd be climbing into her window?

09:34.707 --> 09:36.675
<i>Ah, good point. Risky Business?</i>

09:36.709 --> 09:37.976
No. Hookers don't climb.

09:38.011 --> 09:39.378
<i>Oh, I know, Home Alone.</i>

09:39.412 --> 09:41.013
<i>Home Alone must've had a lattice.</i>

09:41.047 --> 09:43.182
Maybe, but that was 1990.

09:43.216 --> 09:45.084
Eh, it feels like an '80s movie.

09:45.118 --> 09:47.152
You know, it was probably
greenlit in the '80s,

09:47.187 --> 09:48.720
when lattices were still a thing.

09:48.755 --> 09:50.389
Oh, wow, here we are.

09:55.728 --> 09:58.564
All right, Brian, at this size,
this is a two-man job.

09:58.598 --> 10:00.732
While I adjust the settings,
you go over there

10:00.767 --> 10:03.702
and hit the tiny button to fire it up.

10:17.684 --> 10:19.284
Wait a minute.

10:19.319 --> 10:21.720
This doesn't feel right.
What button did you hit?

10:21.754 --> 10:23.755
That one. The tiny button.

10:24.657 --> 10:26.625
Wait, did you hit the tiny button

10:26.659 --> 10:28.227
or the button that says "tiny"?

10:28.261 --> 10:29.728
I hit the button that says "tiny."

10:29.762 --> 10:31.430
- You said, "Hit the tiny button."
- Exactly!

10:31.464 --> 10:33.899
I didn't say, "Hit the big
button that says 'tiny, '"

10:33.933 --> 10:35.234
I said, "hit the tiny button."

10:35.268 --> 10:37.002
The one you pressed
is going to shrink us down

10:37.036 --> 10:38.470
to microscopic size!

10:38.505 --> 10:40.405
Well, why would you make
the tiny button big?

10:40.440 --> 10:43.142
I had to make it big enough
to write "tiny" on it!

10:45.945 --> 10:48.347
Well, what the hell do we do now?!

10:48.381 --> 10:49.781
I don't...

10:49.816 --> 10:51.517
I-I'm still thinking
about that lattice thing.

10:51.551 --> 10:53.051
<i>I want to say Parenthood?</i>

10:53.086 --> 10:56.355
<i>Parenthood. Yes.
I feel like Parenthood is right.</i>

11:17.663 --> 11:19.130
It's beautiful.

11:19.165 --> 11:21.733
Ah, I just wish my hot
girlfriend were here to see it.

11:21.767 --> 11:23.568
Oh, yeah? Yeah, you have a girlfriend?

11:23.602 --> 11:27.705
- What's her name?
- Girly... Friendston.

11:27.740 --> 11:30.375
"Girly Friendston"? Nice try, Stewie.

11:30.409 --> 11:32.377
Why won't he answer my texts?

11:32.411 --> 11:34.379
Girly, your piano teacher's here.

11:34.413 --> 11:36.981
- Oh, Mom, do I have to?
- Girly Friendston,

11:37.016 --> 11:39.317
you stop mooning over
that boyfriend of yours

11:39.351 --> 11:42.220
and get down here this instant.

11:50.629 --> 11:52.397
Hi. I'm the exterminator.

11:52.431 --> 11:55.600
An ex-Terminator?
So you used to be a Terminator?

11:55.634 --> 11:58.570
- No. I kill rats and bugs.
- And Sarah Connor.

11:58.604 --> 12:01.673
- No, Peter. We have a rat.
- My stuff's in my truck.

12:01.707 --> 12:03.808
I'll be back.

12:03.842 --> 12:05.143
See that, Lois?

12:05.177 --> 12:06.978
There's more Terminators around
than you think there are.

12:16.021 --> 12:17.989
I hope he can terminate

12:18.023 --> 12:21.059
some of the bad attitudes
on our kids, huh?

12:21.093 --> 12:23.228
Yeah.

12:29.001 --> 12:31.236
What's that sound?

12:31.270 --> 12:32.804
Oh, my God! Look!

12:47.686 --> 12:49.954
Holy crap, what the hell
were those things?!

12:49.989 --> 12:51.122
Dust mites.

12:51.156 --> 12:53.891
One of the most dominant species
of the micro world.

12:53.926 --> 12:55.260
Why did they just attack like that?

12:55.294 --> 12:56.661
Because they're jerks.

12:56.695 --> 12:59.464
Aah! Who the hell are you?

12:59.498 --> 13:01.432
Sorry. Didn't mean to scare you,
little buddies.

13:01.467 --> 13:03.368
My name's Vernon. I'm a water bear.

13:03.402 --> 13:05.770
A water bear? What's a water bear?

13:05.804 --> 13:07.772
They're predominantly
water-dwelling, eight-legged

13:07.806 --> 13:09.540
segmented micro animals.

13:09.575 --> 13:12.610
They're also known as
a moss piglet or a tardigrade.

13:12.645 --> 13:15.246
You can call me tardy,
but I'm always on time.

13:15.281 --> 13:17.248
Ha-ha. Yeah.

13:26.859 --> 13:29.827
Well, here she is. Home sweet home.

13:29.862 --> 13:31.863
Everybody, we've got guests!

13:35.534 --> 13:38.202
You'll see that we have quite
the diverse cast of characters.

13:38.237 --> 13:40.305
I'm the country water bear.

13:40.339 --> 13:43.308
"Yee-haw" is what I say.

13:43.342 --> 13:45.443
Flagellum? I don't even know them.

13:45.477 --> 13:47.011
I'm the black one.

13:47.046 --> 13:50.615
And I'm Patrick Stewart as a water bear.

13:50.649 --> 13:52.884
I can't believe there's
this whole universe

13:52.918 --> 13:55.687
hidden here in your rug...
where everyone speaks English.

13:55.721 --> 13:57.055
Okay, Brian, take the ride.

13:57.089 --> 14:00.625
Here, have a sip of water.

14:01.827 --> 14:04.762
What the...? Hey, cut it out!

14:04.797 --> 14:06.831
You have water? Water is life.

14:06.865 --> 14:08.833
Yeah, we need water bad.

14:08.867 --> 14:12.370
And I'm the gay one, but I'm
not, like, doing the gay voice.

14:12.404 --> 14:14.472
Listen, Stewie and I come from a place

14:14.506 --> 14:17.008
where water flows like... well, water.

14:17.042 --> 14:18.843
That's right.
And we need to get back there.

14:18.877 --> 14:20.678
And if you guys help us,

14:20.713 --> 14:23.681
we'll make sure you never
want for water again.

14:23.716 --> 14:24.849
What do you say?

14:24.883 --> 14:26.884
All right!

14:26.919 --> 14:28.319
Patrick Stewart!

14:32.358 --> 14:34.959
- Well, what'd you find?
- I'll be honest.

14:34.993 --> 14:37.995
I think this is a conversation
best had over dinner.

14:38.030 --> 14:40.932
Oh. Okay.

14:40.966 --> 14:42.667
So what's going on with the house?

14:42.701 --> 14:44.736
I don't like talking business
at the table.

14:44.770 --> 14:48.106
- Let's just enjoy our wine.
- You're right. I'm sorry.

14:49.908 --> 14:51.342
Your wife's asleep.

14:51.377 --> 14:53.111
Sometimes she fakes it
so I can't hump her,

14:53.145 --> 14:54.946
but this seems legit.

14:54.980 --> 14:58.082
So, uh, shouldn't we talk about
what you found at our house?

14:58.117 --> 15:01.652
I don't know. It's so late.
I have a crazy idea.

15:01.687 --> 15:03.688
Should we talk about it over a nightcap?

15:03.722 --> 15:05.656
Uh, sure, I guess.

15:07.659 --> 15:09.694
I'm a little chilly.

15:09.728 --> 15:12.563
Oh, well, I-I guess I don't need this.

15:15.134 --> 15:18.770
Sir? Sir, I asked you what
you found out about the house.

15:18.804 --> 15:21.739
What? Oh. You're gonna
have to tent the house.

15:21.774 --> 15:24.375
All right. Thanks for your work.
You're very professional.

15:24.410 --> 15:26.778
Yeah, that's me. Professional.

15:26.812 --> 15:28.613
Always professional.

15:29.715 --> 15:31.949
And alone.

15:50.035 --> 15:52.136
What the hell is this giant wall?

15:52.171 --> 15:54.739
We're here, Brian. That's your laptop.

15:54.773 --> 15:57.442
If we get inside, I can remotely
hack into the shrink ray.

16:02.948 --> 16:04.949
Oh, my God! It's the dust mites!

16:07.419 --> 16:10.788
Oh, no! Water Bear Consuela,
can you stop them?

16:10.823 --> 16:13.925
No, no. I only clean Wednesday.

16:13.959 --> 16:17.795
- Can't you just clean today?
- No, no. Wednesday.

16:23.135 --> 16:24.569
Here's the micro board.

16:24.603 --> 16:27.672
I just need to reroute the circuits.

16:32.644 --> 16:35.313
All right. The laptop is now
linked to the shrink ray.

16:35.347 --> 16:37.982
The only problem is that
I can't activate it from here.

16:38.016 --> 16:39.517
We still somehow have to press

16:39.551 --> 16:41.252
the return button on the keyboard.

16:41.286 --> 16:44.088
But at this size, there's no way
I can do it alone.

16:44.122 --> 16:46.257
Wait. I've got an idea.

16:46.291 --> 16:49.060
Well, you better act quickly.

16:51.697 --> 16:54.065
Guys! Follow me up this way!

16:58.270 --> 17:01.172
Why is there a tiny lattice
inside this computer?

17:01.206 --> 17:04.208
I guess Steve Jobs was
really into '80s movies.

17:15.554 --> 17:17.021
Brian, wait for my signal.

17:18.023 --> 17:19.190
Hold.

17:20.292 --> 17:22.126
Hold.

17:23.996 --> 17:25.062
Hold.

17:29.201 --> 17:31.802
- Now!
- You-you never told me what to do.

17:31.837 --> 17:32.870
- Jump!
- Why?

17:32.905 --> 17:35.873
- Trust me.
- Aah!

17:53.125 --> 17:55.059
My God! It worked!

17:55.093 --> 17:56.427
Stewie, you're a genius!

17:56.429 --> 18:00.197
Oh, no.

18:02.067 --> 18:04.235
Run!

18:04.269 --> 18:06.504
Okay. All the gas bombs are set up.

18:06.538 --> 18:09.073
Time to blow all those vermin
to kingdom come.

18:09.107 --> 18:10.675
Can I press the button?

18:10.709 --> 18:14.645
Hmm, perhaps that's a question
best pondered over dinner?

18:14.680 --> 18:16.948
You-you can just press it. Go ahead.

18:24.723 --> 18:26.490
Aah! Poison gas!

18:26.525 --> 18:28.593
They must've gotten
an exterminator for the rat!

18:47.312 --> 18:49.580
Tiny Tom Cruise?

19:08.400 --> 19:12.069
Thank you, Tiny Tom Cruise.
How can we ever repay you?

19:12.104 --> 19:13.771
Well, you could make a sizable donation

19:13.805 --> 19:15.139
to the Church of Spaceship Beep Boop.

19:15.173 --> 19:16.707
You mean the Church of...

19:16.742 --> 19:18.309
Yeah, kidnapping, torture,
extortion, that's the one.

19:18.343 --> 19:19.977
And we won't get in trouble

19:20.012 --> 19:22.213
because we didn't use the actual name.

19:22.247 --> 19:23.581
<i>What did he just say?</i>

19:23.615 --> 19:27.151
<i>We are about love and
spaceships and beep boop!</i>

19:27.185 --> 19:29.253
<i>Get my lawyer on the phone!</i>

19:29.287 --> 19:32.156
- You have children in there?!
- Oh, yeah, three.

19:32.190 --> 19:34.025
Should-should we have mentioned that?

19:37.829 --> 19:41.832
Meg, Chris, come to the light.

19:41.867 --> 19:44.035
Meg, no. Don't do it.

19:44.069 --> 19:45.636
Don't go to Prince!

19:45.671 --> 19:47.805
Come to the purple light, Meg.

19:47.839 --> 19:49.640
Come taste infinity.

19:49.675 --> 19:51.542
Don't listen to him, Meg.

19:51.576 --> 19:55.513
But he's so talented
and he's got so many drugs.

19:55.547 --> 19:57.548
Alan Thicke is here, too.

19:57.582 --> 20:00.351
Hey, guys. Come on in. It's a hoot.

20:00.385 --> 20:02.953
I'm coming, Alan Thicke.

20:02.988 --> 20:04.355
No!

20:04.389 --> 20:07.224
Google my CrystaLight
aerobics competition.

20:07.259 --> 20:09.260
It's ridiculous.

20:15.975 --> 20:18.076
I hope Vernon and the gang survived.

20:18.111 --> 20:19.578
That gas was pretty powerful.

20:19.612 --> 20:22.013
Well, let's take a look.

20:28.315 --> 20:31.251
They're okay.
Let's deliver on our promise.

20:31.285 --> 20:33.653
A little water for our little friends.

20:40.327 --> 20:43.229
- Oh, hell no!
- Set country music!

20:43.264 --> 20:45.832
Oh, my gay God.

20:48.436 --> 20:51.438
Ah, they're dead. Now I'm sad.

20:51.472 --> 20:54.074
Cheer me up, Jean-Claude Van Damme.

21:01.349 --> 21:04.349
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.tv